{
  "kanda": "sundara",
  "sarga": 32,
  "title": "Seetha is shocked to see Hanuma",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/sundara/sarga32/sundarasans32.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/sundara/sarga32/sundaraitrans32.htm",
  "translator": "K. M. K. Murthy",
  "introduction": [
    "Seetha is shocked to see Hanuma, perched on the branches of a shimshupa tree She is confused whether it is a dream or a reality. Finally, she thinks that as the monkey is talking to her in a manifested form, it is quite a reality. She prays Lord Brihaspati and Brahma to make he words spoken by Hanuma as true."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इत्यार्षे श्रीमद्रामायणे आदिकाव्ये सुन्दरकाण्डे द्वात्रिंशः सर्गः",
    "Thus completes 32nd Chapter of Sundara Kanda of the glorious Ramayana of Valmiki, the work of a sage and the oldest epic"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "5.32.1",
      "label": "5.32.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "ततः शाखा अन्तरे लीनम् दृष्ट्वा चलित मानसा |\nवेष्टितार्जुनवस्त्रम् तं विद्युत्सम्घातपिङ्गलम् ||",
      "iast": "tataḥ śākhā antare līnam dṛṣṭvā calita mānasā |\nveṣṭitārjunavastram taṃ vidyutsamghātapiṇ^galam ||",
      "translation": "Then, seeing Hanuma, who was tawny coloured like a series of flashing thunderbolts wrapped up in a white cloth and hiding behind the branches of a tree, Seetha had her mind shaken.",
